# leaderboard.zd — exercises the pipeline, conditionals, and nested types.
#
# This file was un-writable until the standard library landed. `table at
# player.name` correctly yields `Option of Whole` (spec §5.4: indexing is
# bounds-checked, unlike TypeScript's unchecked lookup), and `Option` can
# only be eliminated by `when`, which is a statement — so there was no way
# to unwrap one inside an expression such as a sort key. §14F.2a recorded
# the consequence in the type checker's own words: *no program can read a
# map and use the result.*
#
# `atOr` is the fix, and it is an ordinary ZDeceptron function over an
# ordinary `when` (`prelude/map.zd`, `prelude/option.zd`) rather than a
# grammar change.
#
# Written specifically to stress parts of the grammar the other examples
# do not touch: every pipeline clause, `if`/`otherwise`, comparison
# operators, boolean word operators, and nested collection types.

state scores    is durable Map of Text to Whole starting empty
state minScore  is client  Whole                starting 0
state showAll   is client  Truth                starting no
state search    is client  Text                 starting ""

# The list the pipeline below draws from. A pipeline's `from` names a
# signal like any other expression does, so the source has to exist.
state players   is durable List of Player       starting empty

# Every pipeline clause in one function, reading top to bottom.
state ranked is server List of Text from rankPlayers with scores, minScore, showAll

function rankPlayers with table, floor, includeInactive
    from players
    keep each player where player.active or includeInactive
    keep each player where (scoreOf with table is table, player is player) >= floor
    sort each player by scoreOf with table is table, player is player
    map each player to player.name
    take first 25

# A player with no entry in the table has not scored, which is zero. That
# is the decision `Option` forces a program to make and §5.4 exists to
# stop it being made silently.
function scoreOf with table, player
    give atOr with table is table, key is player.name, fallback is 0

# Conditionals and comparison operators.
function tierFor with points
    if points >= 1000
        give "gold"
    otherwise
        if points >= 500
            give "silver"
        otherwise
            give "bronze"

# Nested collection types.
state groups  is durable Map of Text to List of Player starting empty
state history is durable List of List of Whole         starting empty

view
    Column
        Heading "Leaderboard"

        Row
            Input search, hint is "filter by name"
            Checkbox showAll, label is "include inactive"

        when ranked
            Loading           show Spinner
            Failed with error show ErrorBar message is error.message
            Ready with list
                each player in list
                    Row player, padding is 8
                        Button "promote"
                            on click
                                add 100 to scores at player
